ROUND 2 PATCH (not yet applied) — screen-change feedback

Rationale: baseline failures are dominated by blind clicking (13 of 19 calls in a
typical failed episode were clicks). The agent cannot tell that its click did
nothing, so it clicks again somewhere else. Telling it "the screen did not change"
is cheap, domain-general, and targets the observed failure directly.

In _encode(), after producing the frame:

    import hashlib
    digest = hashlib.sha256(shot).hexdigest() if shot else None
    if entry is not None:
        if digest and entry.get("last_digest") == digest:
            payload["screen_unchanged"] = True
        entry["last_digest"] = digest

In computerTools screenshotResult():

    if (result.screen_unchanged) {
      lines.push(
        'The screen is pixel-identical to before your last action, so that action had '
        + 'no visible effect. Do not simply repeat it. Work out why: wrong target, page '
        + 'still loading, something covering the element, or focus elsewhere.',
      );
    }

Caveat to check when applied: a page with a blinking cursor or animation will never
hash identical, so this under-reports rather than over-reports. That is the safe
direction — it will never wrongly tell the agent nothing happened.
